
NAME
	_printf

SYNOPSIS

	#include "main.h"

	int _printf(const char *format, ...);

DESCRIPTION
	_printf
	function produces output according to a format string, writing to standard output.

	Format Specifiers
	A conversion specifier is introduced by the % character:

	%c: Print a single character.

	%s: Prints a null-terminated string. If argument is NULL, print "(null)".

	%
